171
00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:21.900
You've worked at Binance FTX CoinCall.

172
00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:28.420
And CoinCall is different because it's focusing on options and futures, right?

173
00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:29.280
Yes.

174
00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:32.420
These are very complicated financial tools.

175
00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:37.440
Can you explain to us in very simple terms, what are the differences between these two?

176
00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:42.740
The main difference between futures and options trading is that futures are a contract that

177
00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:48.380
obligates, that's very important, the buyer to purchase or sell an asset at a specified

178
00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:51.020
date, okay, and price.

179
00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:57.620
While options give the buyer the right, but not the obligation to purchase or sell this asset

180
00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:00.400
at a specified price and time.

181
00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.660
So basically with futures, you have the obligation.

182
00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:04.840
With options, you don't have the obligation.

183
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.940
You have the right to buy something in the future.

184
00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:15.700
If we talk about personality, how would you describe the different personality between

185
00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:18.380
like an option trader and a futures trader?

186
00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:23.340
I would say futures is a short-term trader, maybe.

187
00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:25.720
For options, I would say that is more long-term.

188
00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:27.940
Options are less risky than futures.

189
00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:32.520
So probably someone who's less risk averse will prefer options.

190
00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:40.840
So almost all crypto exchanges offer perpetual contracts, right?

191
00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:45.360
So a lot of people in crypto, they're more used to this tool.

192
00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:49.860
But why aren't more exchanges offering options trading?

193
00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:51.580
I think it was a trend.

194
00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:57.660
So before Binance made futures mainstream, because I think it was Binance in 2020, futures were

195
00:10:57.660 --> 00:10:59.560
already available on BitMEX, for example.

196
00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.640
Yeah, it's just a matter of the timing.

197
00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:06.300
If back then Binance decided to start with options rather than futures, we'd be talking

198
00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:09.040
right now that futures is the next thing and everything.

199
00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:10.980
So you don't think options are harder?

200
00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:13.840
I think that maybe you have more things to learn in options.

201
00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:17.860
If you already know futures, options shouldn't be very difficult.

202
00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:20.820
If you're starting from zero, it's new content from you.

203
00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:23.280
So it's the same if you learn options and if you learn futures.

204
00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:34.640
I come across this Bloomberg report that says options are the next big thing or is already

205
00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:36.820
